│ (apremilast: -4.3 ± 5.1; placebo: -0.8 ± 4.5; P = 0.0004) and in reducing activity impairment (apremilast: -11.0 ±   │
│ 22.3; placebo: 2.5 ± 25.5; P = 0.0063). CONCLUSION Despite the absence of a significant difference between           │
│ apremilast and placebo in proportion of patients achieving a PPPGA of 0/1, the presence of significant differences   │
│ observed for several secondary endpoints suggests that apremilast may have a role in the treatment of                │
│ moderate-to-severe palmoplantar psoriasis."}, {"study_index": 93, "title": "Efficacy and safety of itolizumab, a     │
